Menu Page – Review Section Improvements
    -Center-align the "review-item-block" element.
    -Add star icons to display the average rating of the menu.
      → Place this right under the menu name inside the "review-item-block".
    -The Add to Cart button does not seem to be adding the item to the cart (bug).
    -In each review card:  
        -Below the menu info, make the username of the reviewer clickable.  
        -Clicking it should redirect to that user's profile page.
        -Before the rating number (e.g. "4.2/5"), display star icons that visually represent the rating.
    -Track whether the current user has already reviewed this menu:  
        -If the user has not reviewed it → show button labeled "Submit"  
        -If the user has already reviewed it → change the button text to "Edit"  
        -When clicking "Edit", the form should load and update the existing review instead of creating a new one.

Additional Question
Do we currently have a function (or backend logic) to:
    -Calculate the individual rating for each review, and  
    -Compute the average rating for each menu?

If not (or if it's missing/incomplete), consider updating the Meal API (in data/meal.js or the related backend/service) to:
    Store and maintain the following fields for each menu/meal document:
     -totalRating → sum of all rating values (e.g. number like 23 for five 5-star + three 4-star + …)
     -reviewCount → total number of reviews/ratings received (number of reviewers)
     -averageRating → pre-calculated average (e.g. totalRating / reviewCount, rounded to 1–2 decimal places)

